    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0578" n="474" xml:id="pg474"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.00 Revolutions/176: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-08-02T10:00:00-05:00">August 2, 1932—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>159. Peña Villalón, Minister of the Interior and Minister of Lands and
                    Colonization; Soto Rengifo, Minister of Education; and Toro, Minister of Labor,
                    resigned yesterday. New appointments are: Josephus Fernandez, Minister of
                    Interior; Luis David Cruz Ocampo, Minister of Education; Juan B. Rossetti,
                    Minister of Labor. These changes are away from the Left.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
